WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.769
-We are so luck to have
our friend, Fred Armisen,

00:00:02.769 --> 00:00:04.170
leading the band all the week.

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:05.304
It's great to see you, Fred.

00:00:05.304 --> 00:00:08.674
-Hi.
-It's so fun to have you here,

00:00:08.674 --> 00:00:10.343
because you can always keep me
up to date

00:00:10.343 --> 00:00:11.878
on your other projects.

00:00:11.878 --> 00:00:13.279
But this one, I had to see,

00:00:13.279 --> 00:00:15.348
because you've sort of been
doing a bit of a press tour.

00:00:15.348 --> 00:00:16.649
I saw you on
"Good Morning America",

00:00:16.649 --> 00:00:18.884
I saw you on NBC's very own
"Today Show",

00:00:18.884 --> 00:00:21.987
announcing that you have
a competing holiday

00:00:21.987 --> 00:00:25.191
with Valentine's Day
that you're starting this year.

00:00:25.191 --> 00:00:26.259
-That's right.

00:00:26.259 --> 00:00:28.094
[ Laughter ]

00:00:28.094 --> 00:00:31.398
-We would love -- I think we
would all love to hear about it.

00:00:31.398 --> 00:00:33.999
-It's called Acquaintance Day.
-Okay.

00:00:33.999 --> 00:00:36.735
-So we're just celebrating
people that you know

00:00:36.735 --> 00:00:39.505
kind of well, you know, you see
them once in a while

00:00:39.505 --> 00:00:41.073
every couple of years.
-Okay.

00:00:41.073 --> 00:00:43.542
-And those are really important
relationships --

00:00:43.542 --> 00:00:45.111
you know, people you don't know
their last names,

00:00:45.111 --> 00:00:47.247
but you just recognize
their face.

00:00:47.247 --> 00:00:50.516
And it's just a celebration,
so, you know,

00:00:50.516 --> 00:00:52.918
we're just trying to find a way
for people to send cards --

00:00:52.918 --> 00:00:55.321
find their address first
then send the card.

00:00:55.321 --> 00:00:57.757
-Right, I would imagine finding
an address is difficult

00:00:57.757 --> 00:00:59.725
if you don't know
a person's last name.

00:00:59.725 --> 00:01:03.095
-It's difficult, but at the same
time, that's the fun of it.

00:01:03.095 --> 00:01:05.998
You know, it's that exploration
of, like, trying to find

00:01:05.998 --> 00:01:07.600
that person -- "Oh, there you
are, you know.

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:09.234
Let's celebrate
Acquaintance Day."

00:01:09.234 --> 00:01:10.536
-And now what -- wait.

00:01:10.536 --> 00:01:12.605
So, example, if Hallmark made
an Acquaintance Day card

00:01:12.605 --> 00:01:14.507
and I open it up,
what would it say inside,

00:01:14.507 --> 00:01:17.076
like, what's the sort of
the text on those?

00:01:17.076 --> 00:01:19.445
-"Remember the time we saw
each other?

00:01:19.445 --> 00:01:21.480
Those times are always great.

00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:23.182
The times that we saw
each other's faces

00:01:23.182 --> 00:01:24.784
we'll always, always remember.

00:01:24.784 --> 00:01:29.388
You're special to me
once every two years.

00:01:29.388 --> 00:01:31.557
Thinking of you
this whole week."

00:01:31.557 --> 00:01:32.925
It's that kind of thing.

00:01:32.925 --> 00:01:33.926
-That's really good.

00:01:33.926 --> 00:01:35.294
I'm so excited --
Acquaintance Day.

00:01:35.294 --> 00:01:38.932
Look out, Valentine's Day,
a-look out.

